  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+2\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $2({\\lambda }_{2}-{\\lambda }_{1}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+2\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{\u2015}{\\lambda }}_{1}=4-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }_{2}-{\\lambda }_{1}) & =2(4-2\\text{i}-(4+2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(-4\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
